<H2 ALIGN=CENTER>ACCESS &amp; GENERAL INFORMATION <HR></H2>

<P>Shonan Village Center is conveniently located for access to
Tokyo and Narita and Haneda Airports. Take JR (Japan Railway)
from the Narita Airport station to Zushi, via Tokyo.<BR>
At Zushi station, take a local bus bound for Shonan Village Center,
or take a Taxi. Renting a car is not recommended.</P>

<P ALIGN=CENTER><IMG SRC="wide.map-E.jpeg" WIDTH="262" HEIGHT="217"
ALIGN="BOTTOM" NATURALSIZEFLAG="3"></P>

<UL>
  <LI>From Narita Airport to Zushi station
  <P>JR serves two types of trains from the airport: Narita Express
  (N'EX) and Airport Narita. In general, whichever type of train
  you can catch first will take you to Zushi earliest.<BR>
<BR>
  About 150 minutes by JR Narita Express and Yokosuka line.<BR>
  Narita Express (N'EX) is a limited express train bound for Shinjuku,
  Yokohama or Ofuna, departing every 30 minutes or an hour. Please
  take one for Yokohama or Ofuna. At the final stop, transfer to
  a JR Yokosuka-line local train to Zushi (7 stops from Yokohama,
  3 stops from Ofuna).<BR>
  A JR ticket to Zushi will cost &yen;2,210. Only one-way tickets
  are available.<BR>
  All N'EX seats need reservation. Please reserve a seat at a ticket
  counter when you buy a ticket to Zushi. A limited express supplement
  (&yen;2,290) will be charged in addition to the basic fare.<BR>
<BR>
  Airport Narita, a JR Sobu &amp; Yokosuka-line rapid ('kaisoku')
  train, departs hourly and most of the services go directly to
  Zushi in 150 minutes. (Some go beyond Zushi to Yokosuka or Kurihama.
  Some go only to Tokyo or Ofuna, in which case please transfer
  to the next Yokosuka-line train at the final stop.) Airport Narita
  does not require supplement, but a suggestion to tourists is
  to take a Green Car (first-class accommodations) in the middle
  of a train and pay a supplement (&yen;1,620) on board.
</UL>

<MENU>
  <LI>From Tokyo to Zushi station
  <P>About 90 minutes from Tokyo by JR Yokosuka line.
</MENU>

<DIR>
  <LI>From Haneda Airport to Zushi
  <P>Take a Keihin Kyuko line to Yokohama station and transfer
  to Yokosuka line train to Zushi.<BR>
<BR>
  <IMG SRC="transp.chart-E.gif" WIDTH="322" HEIGHT="299" ALIGN="BOTTOM"
  NATURALSIZEFLAG="3">
  <LI>From Zushi station to the Shonan Village Center
  <P>Take a bus for SHONAN VILLAGE CENTER or SHONAN VILLAGE BUS
  TERMINAL at the No.1 bus-stop in front of JR Zushi station, and
  get off at the Shonan Village Center bus-stop. It takes about
  30 minutes.<BR>
